SUMMARY:Easy Peasy MST\, 5.5 or 7.5 miles
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nPlease read the entire description
 . There is a choice.\n\nWe'll start at the parking lot at Fresh Market\, H
 endersonville Rd.\, take the spur trail\, which is a little tricky\, to MS
 T\, and head west to the bridge at Dingle Creek\, which is our turn around
 . The trail has been immaculately restored after Helene. Also\, sections t
 hat were heavily forested with a dense upper canopy are now amazingly open
 ed to the sky.\n\nThis is not a difficult hike. It's a smooth trail with g
 radual elevation. We'll hike at a slow pace\, between 2.0 and 2.5 mph. Out
  and back is about 5.5 miles. Expect to spend 2.5 to 3.0 hours hiking on t
 he trail.\n\n**For those wanting a longer hike Craig-like hike**\, you can
  take off after Dingle Creek and hike down to the new bridge over I-26. Th
 ere and back to Fresh Market is approx. 7. 5 miles. The MST at the new bri
 dge is currently closed--construction/landscaping.\n\n**Park near Henderso
 nville Rd.\, away from Haywood Appliance**.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/314683212
 /
