DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260516T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260516T134500
SUMMARY:Scenic AVL  - Waynesville Way - Weekend Wildcard
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nCarpooling: Please announce in the
  chat if you would like to carpool. I recommend 8:55 from 16 Regent Park B
 lvd\, Asheville (near Sam's Club)\, but I am coming from Hendersonville\, 
 so I won't be there.\n\nRating: Strenuous for Distance\nDistance: 9 miles\
 nElevation Gain: 1000 feet\, in small chunks\nFeatures: Farmer's Market\, 
 Rural farm views\, neighborhood charm\, nice downtown.\nWildlife: No bears
 \, but there are lots of birds and a few cows.\nPace: 3.2 mph when moving\
 , but we will stop here and there.\nSurface: Road\nDogs: On leash\nRoute (
 reverse direction): [Waynesville Way](https://www.alltrails.com/explore/re
 cording/activity-november-11-2024-5e38810)\n[.](https://maps.app.goo.gl/dr
 FxX2TaTrZKWX9F8)\nCoffee Break: We are walking the route in the opposite d
 irection from how we usually do it . We will stop for a break at the Farme
 r's Market at the Shelton House Museum.\n**[Special Instructions](https://
 maps.app.goo.gl/3LZwYE6S8TJRgXpQ6?g_st=ac)**[: If you are late\, meet us](
 https://maps.app.goo.gl/3LZwYE6S8TJRgXpQ6?g_st=ac) at the Shelton House fa
 rmers market\; we will arrive in 45 minutes from the start time (10:15).\n
 \nNo bathroom at the start. but there's woods.\n\n\\*Mountain Research Sta
 tion: We are walking down Test Farm Road across the NC Agricultural Extens
 ion Mountain Research Station. Please sign in using the [Visitor Registrat
 ion](https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfDFCDqvA7x7AkL8A2jaLthTf2lS
 QBwlEyC99r-H4SVDsqQaA/viewform) website.\n\nScenic Asheville Series: This 
 hike is a wildcard \, meaning that it can be a substitute for any of the o
 ther hikes.\nThere are [10 hikes ](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/
 1XUm-X1_OhxKIi8JU5rhjsW37cAl4yYx8yB_NEjjI5Lk/edit?usp=drivesdk)in the seri
 es\; hike 9 of them and receive an [attractive badge ](https://docs.google
 .com/drawings/d/1goXUXfzUBqhB4_UeCxodlk4ZPeCCgqZrWK2EUJvk_vI/edit)for your
  pack. Badgers can always attend a hike\, even if on the waiting list. See
  our [highlights here](https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/18cFp2Uhw8Xt
 hOFXxekBpt2LGP6ww-V7kmXQExI7Y0h0/)!\n\nRSVP and On-Time Start:\n\n* Call (
 do not text) the hike leader on the day of the hike if you can't find the 
 start 828-290-0886\n\\*If you decide you cannot come\, please change your 
 RSVP.\n\nDisclaimer and Release of Liability:\nThis activity involves hiki
 ng on city streets that may have traffic. Participants are responsible for
  their safety on streets and trails. The organizer of this trip is a volun
 teer and not a professional guide. The function of the organizer is only t
 o organize this trip. If you sign up or participate in this event you ackn
 owledge that you freely and voluntarily agree to assume all risks of injur
 ies\, illnesses\, and damages arising from\, as a result of\, and associat
 ed with this event. In addition\, you acknowledge that you agree to the Me
 etup terms: [https://www.meetup.com/terms](https://www.meetup.com/terms)
